IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `iana-types`
IMPORT `iana-employment`
IMPORT `iana-penalty`
IMPORT `iana-offence`
IMPORT `iana-goal`

-- Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006 (UK) — the encoder's tests.
-- Expected values are worked by hand from the Act.

§ `Tests`

GIVEN p IS AN `Immigration position`
GIVETH AN `Employment facts`
`an adult with` p MEANS
    `Employment facts` OF Date 1 1 1990, Date 1 3 2025, Date 31 5 2025, TRUE, p

GIVEN dob IS A DATE, until IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Employment facts`
`someone born` dob `employed until` until MEANS
    `Employment facts` OF dob, Date 1 1 2025, until, TRUE, `no leave to enter or remain`

illegal MEANS `an adult with` `no leave to enter or remain`

§§ `Goal 1 — employment contrary to s 15`

#ASSERT `the employment is contrary to s 15 in` illegal
#ASSERT `the employment is contrary to s 15 in` (`an adult with` `leave that is invalid`)
#ASSERT `the employment is contrary to s 15 in` (`an adult with` `leave that has ceased to have effect`)
#ASSERT `the employment is contrary to s 15 in` (`an adult with` `leave with a condition preventing this employment`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the employment is contrary to s 15 in` (`an adult with` `leave permitting this employment`))
#ASSERT NOT (`the employment is contrary to s 15 in` (`an adult with` `not subject to immigration control`))
-- s 24: immigration bail.
#ASSERT `the employment is contrary to s 15 in` (`an adult with` `immigration bail with a restriction preventing this employment`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the employment is contrary to s 15 in` (`an adult with` `immigration bail without such a restriction`))
-- s 25(b): not under a contract of service or apprenticeship.
#ASSERT NOT (`the employment is contrary to s 15 in` (`Employment facts` OF Date 1 1 1990, Date 1 3 2025, Date 31 5 2025, FALSE, `no leave to enter or remain`))
-- s 25(a): 16th birthday on 10 June 2025.
#ASSERT NOT (`the employment is contrary to s 15 in` (`someone born` (Date 10 6 2009) `employed until` (Date 9 6 2025)))
#ASSERT `the employment is contrary to s 15 in` (`someone born` (Date 10 6 2009) `employed until` (Date 10 6 2025))
-- Born 29 February 2008: 16 on 29 February 2024.
#ASSERT `the employment is contrary to s 15 in` (`someone born` (Date 29 2 2008) `employed until` (Date 29 2 2024))
#ASSERT NOT (`the employment is contrary to s 15 in` (`someone born` (Date 29 2 2008) `employed until` (Date 28 2 2024)))

§§ `Goal 2 — the civil penalty`

-- Fields: complied, knew, maximum, amount, given on, objection.
GIVEN complied IS A BOOLEAN, knew IS A BOOLEAN, amount IS A NUMBER, o IS AN `Objection outcome`
GIVETH A `Penalty facts`
`penalty, complied` complied `, knew` knew `, amount` amount `, objection` o MEANS
    `Penalty facts` OF complied, knew, 60000, amount, Date 3 2 2025, o

basic MEANS `penalty, complied` FALSE `, knew` FALSE `, amount` 45000 `, objection` `no objection given`
#ASSERT `a penalty notice may be given for` illegal `with` basic
#ASSERT `the penalty payable for` illegal `with` basic EQUALS 45000
-- Over the prescribed maximum.
#ASSERT NOT (`a penalty notice may be given for` illegal `with` (`penalty, complied` FALSE `, knew` FALSE `, amount` 70000 `, objection` `no objection given`))
-- s 15(3): excused; (4): not if it knew.
#ASSERT `the penalty payable for` illegal `with` (`penalty, complied` TRUE `, knew` FALSE `, amount` 45000 `, objection` `no objection given`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the penalty payable for` illegal `with` (`penalty, complied` TRUE `, knew` TRUE `, amount` 45000 `, objection` `no objection given`) EQUALS 45000
-- Lawful employment.
#ASSERT `the penalty payable for` (`an adult with` `leave permitting this employment`) `with` basic EQUALS 0
-- s 16(4)(a): cancelled.
#ASSERT `the penalty payable for` illegal `with` (`penalty, complied` FALSE `, knew` FALSE `, amount` 45000 `, objection` `penalty cancelled`) EQUALS 0

-- s 15(6)(c): given 3 February 2025, pay-by at the earliest 3 March 2025.
#ASSERT `the earliest pay-by date for` basic EQUALS Date 3 3 2025

-- s 17(4A)-(4E)
#ASSERT `the last day to appeal for` basic EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the last day to appeal for` (`penalty, complied` FALSE `, knew` FALSE `, amount` 45000 `, objection` `penalty cancelled`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the last day to appeal for` (`penalty, complied` FALSE `, knew` FALSE `, amount` 45000 `, objection` (`penalty reduced or no action, decision given on` (Date 10 4 2025))) EQUALS JUST (Date 7 5 2025)
#ASSERT `the last day to appeal for` (`penalty, complied` FALSE `, knew` FALSE `, amount` 50000 `, objection` (`penalty increased by a new notice given on` (Date 20 2 2028))) EQUALS JUST (Date 18 3 2028)
#ASSERT `the last day to appeal for` (`penalty, complied` FALSE `, knew` FALSE `, amount` 45000 `, objection` (`no decision, the period ended on` (Date 15 12 2025))) EQUALS JUST (Date 11 1 2026)

§§ `Goal 3 — the offence`

-- Fields: knew, reasonable cause, jurisdiction, convicted, general limit.
GIVEN knew IS A BOOLEAN, cause IS A BOOLEAN, j IS A `Jurisdiction`, convicted IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Offence facts`
`offence, knew` knew `, cause` cause `, in` j `, convicted` convicted MEANS
    `Offence facts` OF knew, cause, j, convicted, 12

#ASSERT `an offence under s 21 is committed in` illegal `with` (`offence, knew` TRUE `, cause` FALSE `, in` `England and Wales` `, convicted` (Date 1 6 2025))
#ASSERT `an offence under s 21 is committed in` illegal `with` (`offence, knew` FALSE `, cause` TRUE `, in` `England and Wales` `, convicted` (Date 1 6 2025))
#ASSERT NOT (`an offence under s 21 is committed in` illegal `with` (`offence, knew` FALSE `, cause` FALSE `, in` `England and Wales` `, convicted` (Date 1 6 2025)))
#ASSERT NOT (`an offence under s 21 is committed in` (`an adult with` `leave permitting this employment`) `with` (`offence, knew` TRUE `, cause` TRUE `, in` `England and Wales` `, convicted` (Date 1 6 2025)))
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment on indictment, in months` EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment on summary conviction, in months, for` (`offence, knew` TRUE `, cause` FALSE `, in` `England and Wales` `, convicted` (Date 2 5 2022)) EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment on summary conviction, in months, for` (`offence, knew` TRUE `, cause` FALSE `, in` `England and Wales` `, convicted` (Date 1 5 2022)) EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment on summary conviction, in months, for` (`offence, knew` TRUE `, cause` FALSE `, in` `Scotland` `, convicted` (Date 1 6 2025)) EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment on summary conviction, in months, for` (`offence, knew` TRUE `, cause` FALSE `, in` `Northern Ireland` `, convicted` (Date 1 6 2025)) EQUALS 6

§§ `The top-level goal`

pos MEANS `the illegal working position for` (`Illegal working case` OF illegal, JUST basic, JUST (`offence, knew` TRUE `, cause` FALSE `, in` `England and Wales` `, convicted` (Date 1 6 2025)))
#ASSERT pos's `contrary to s 15`
#ASSERT pos's `penalty payable` EQUALS JUST 45000
#ASSERT pos's `earliest pay-by date` EQUALS JUST (Date 3 3 2025)
#ASSERT pos's `last day to appeal` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT pos's `offence committed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT pos's `maximum imprisonment on indictment, in months` EQUALS JUST 60
#ASSERT pos's `maximum imprisonment on summary conviction, in months` EQUALS JUST 12
lawful MEANS `the illegal working position for` (`Illegal working case` OF (`an adult with` `leave permitting this employment`), NOTHING, JUST (`offence, knew` TRUE `, cause` FALSE `, in` `Scotland` `, convicted` (Date 1 6 2025)))
#ASSERT NOT (lawful's `contrary to s 15`)
#ASSERT lawful's `offence committed` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT lawful's `maximum imprisonment on summary conviction, in months` EQUALS NOTHING
